# Shared HTML pages

This repo is GitHub Pages for `mohdizzudin.github.io`.

## Path convention

- Put standalone analysis, ranking, report, and shareable HTML under `shared/`.
- Public URL: `https://mohdizzudin.github.io/shared/{filename}.html`
- Example: `shared/phone.html` → `https://mohdizzudin.github.io/shared/phone.html`

## Rules for agents

- When creating or updating a shareable HTML page, write it to `shared/{slug}.html`.
- Use a short lowercase slug with hyphens (e.g. `phone`, `flagship-ranking`). Prefer `.html`.
- Do not place new analysis HTML at the repo root.
- Do not overwrite unrelated files under `shared/` unless the user names that file.
- After the user asks to deploy, publish, push, or share: commit, push to `master`, and reply with the live `shared/` URL.
- GitHub Pages source is `master` at `/`. A push to `master` publishes `shared/*.html` after the Pages build finishes.

## What stays outside shared/

- Site chrome and app pages may stay at root or in existing folders (`index.html`, `trip/`, `checklist/`, `assets/`, etc.).
- Only shareable analysis / one-off HTML reports use `shared/`.
